1
00:00:00,090 --> 00:00:01,310
You have one heart.

2
00:00:01,310 --> 00:00:02,940
An octopus has...

3
00:00:02,940 --> 00:00:03,900
THREE.

4
00:00:03,940 --> 00:00:04,527
Two of them

5
00:00:04,527 --> 00:00:06,480
are just for its gills.

6
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:07,842
Its blue blood

7
00:00:07,842 --> 00:00:10,130
squeezes through the gills...

8
00:00:10,130 --> 00:00:10,720
and comes out

9
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:11,800
all floppy.

10
00:00:11,853 --> 00:00:12,772
So heart number three

11
00:00:12,772 --> 00:00:14,667
pumps it all over again.

12
00:00:14,710 --> 00:00:15,950
You do this too.

13
00:00:15,950 --> 00:00:18,020
Your heart's just two pumps...

14
00:00:18,020 --> 00:00:19,300
glued together.

15
00:00:19,350 --> 00:00:20,319
But when an octopus

16
00:00:20,319 --> 00:00:21,160
swims...

17
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:22,390
its big heart

18
00:00:22,390 --> 00:00:23,478
STOPS.

19
00:00:23,478 --> 00:00:24,840
For a moment.

20
00:00:24,987 --> 00:00:27,033
So it would rather walk.

21
00:00:27,070 --> 00:00:28,447
Three hearts...

22
00:00:28,447 --> 00:00:29,247
and it still

23
00:00:29,247 --> 00:00:30,867
skips cardio.

